# Build context for the backend image is the repository root, so this file
# governs what gets uploaded to ACR. Keep it tight: everything here is
# either irrelevant to the image, or must never be baked into one.

# Tenant configuration and secrets — never into an image
.azure
**/.env
!**/.env.example
**/*.local.md

# EXCEPTION, and a deliberate one: backend/.env travels into the image.
#
# Why: `azd deploy` updates the image only. Container app environment
# variables come from the Bicep template during `azd provision`, so a key
# supplied through azd env needs a provision to reach the app. Where the
# operator cannot provision — MFA policy, Key Vault access — that path is
# closed, and baking the file into the image is what remains.
#
# Safe because backend/.env is gitignored: the key reaches a private ACR,
# never GitHub. config.py loads it with override=False, so anything the
# platform sets still wins.
#
# Weaker than the alternatives, and worth saying plainly: anyone who can
# pull the image can read the key, and rotation means rebuilding. Prefer
# the Key Vault reference (compassSecretName) or the azd parameter
# (compassApiKey) as soon as either is available.
!backend/.env

# Not needed by the backend image
frontend
infra
scripts
docs
.github
*.md

# Python build noise
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.state

# Node build noise — large, would slow the ACR upload
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out

# VCS and editor
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea
